# night
:night
?if actions_left() == 3
  It is a little after nine. The rain has not eased. It is pouring from the gutters of the rue Saint-Jacques in long glassy ropes, and there is a noise of drums to the south, a very long way off, that comes and goes with the wind.
?elif actions_left() == 2
  It is past midnight. Somewhere on the south road the whole of the army of the faubourg is marching, in the dark, in the sleet, with a king for a hostage, and does not know it.
?else
  It is half past four in the morning. The rain has changed to sleet. There is one thing more that you can do before the day.
?end
* Take a post horse for Versailles, where the women are marching [once] ?if actions_left() > 0
  ~> versailles
  $ do act()
* Go to the Porte Saint-Jacques, where the Avignon courier will come in [once] ?if actions_left() > 0
